// Dotfiles-root ignore patterns, shared across hosts.
//
// Included from ~/dots/.stignore via a folder-relative path:
//     #include syncthing/.dotsignore
//
// Why a separate file: Syncthing never syncs .stignore, so a rule written there
// lives on one host only. This file is committed, so a rule added here reaches
// every host on the next git pull. Keep host-specific overrides in .stignore.
//
// Syntax: https://docs.syncthing.net/users/ignoring.html
// Prefix: ! = include (override), (?d) = deletable

// ===== Per-host, application-generated =====
// DMS regenerates this from the compositor's live outputs, so each host must
// keep its own copy. Syncing it gives the laptop the desktop's monitor layout.
niri/.config/niri/dms/outputs.kdl

// Backups left behind when DMS rewrites niri's config.
(?d)niri/.config/niri/config.kdl.backup*

// ===== DMS runtime state =====
(?d)DankMaterialShell/.config/DankMaterialShell/.firstlaunch
(?d)DankMaterialShell/.config/DankMaterialShell/.changelog-*
// Plugin-manager state: git clones, their symlinks, and repo bookkeeping.
// Not (?d) — re-cloning a plugin is not free, so never let a remote delete it.
DankMaterialShell/.config/DankMaterialShell/plugins

// ===== fish =====
// Universal variables, rewritten at runtime and holding machine-local paths.
fish/.config/fish/fish_variables
